<div class="wrap">
  <div class="sample">Fictional sample. Juniper Reformer Studio is made up, and every name and number is example data, not a customer result.</div>

  <header class="hello">
    <div class="when">A sample monthly letter · Pilates and yoga studios · Naté Hailu, Lubbock</div>
    <h1>What's been on your mind about your studio lately?</h1>
    <p>Pick the one that sounds most like you. You'll see what it looks like in a studio's data, what's usually behind it, and what it may be costing, using your own numbers.</p>
    <div class="chips" role="group" aria-label="Choose what's on your mind">
      <button class="chip" id="c-miss" data-p="miss" aria-pressed="true">Regulars drift away</button>
      <button class="chip" id="c-intro" data-p="intro" aria-pressed="false">Intro clients don't join</button>
      <button class="chip" id="c-packs" data-p="packs" aria-pressed="false">Packs go unused</button>
      <button class="chip" id="c-class" data-p="class" aria-pressed="false">Some classes full, others quiet</button>
      <button class="chip" id="c-nums" data-p="nums" aria-pressed="false">I don't know my numbers</button>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="card" aria-live="polite"><div class="path" id="path"></div></section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Could you handle this yourself?</h2>
    <p class="sub">You might. Whether you work with me or not, here's how I'd approach it.</p>
    <div class="steps3" id="steps"></div>
    <p class="sub" style="margin:14px 0 0">If your software and team already do this every month, you don't need me, and I'll tell you. If it keeps slipping through the cracks, that's what the monthly letter is for. I check your exports, explain what changed, suggest up to three actions with message ideas, and talk it through with whoever will act. You send the messages yourself.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>What you can trust about this page</h2>
    <div class="trust">
      <div><b>It's a made-up studio.</b> Juniper and every client name are fictional, so you can see the format. No real studio's data.</div>
      <div><b>No promise of more clients.</b> The letter shows what happened and suggests next steps. It can't prove why someone stopped coming.</div>
      <div><b>Minimal data.</b> No card numbers, bank details or health notes. Nothing is shared until we agree in writing how files are handled.</div>
      <div><b>One clear price.</b> $300 a month for one location, no long-term commitment. A qualified studio can try one letter free first.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <h2>Want to see if this fits your studio?</h2>
    <p>A 15-minute chat, by phone or in person. I'll ask how you use your reports today, and if there's no real gap, I'll say so. If a partner helps decide, bring them along or send them this page.</p>
    <div class="contact">
      <span class="phone">(832) 507-6699</span>
      <button class="btn pri" id="copyNum" type="button">Copy number</button>
      <a class="btn" href="tel:+18325076699">Call</a>
      <a class="btn" href="sms:+18325076699">Text</a>
      <button class="btn" id="copyLink" type="button">Copy link to share</button>
    </div>
    <div style="font-size:15px;user-select:all;opacity:.9">nat3official@icloud.com</div>
    <div class="toast" id="toast" role="status"></div>
  </section>

  <div class="sample">Below is the full fictional letter a studio owner would get each month.</div>

  <header class="hello" id="letter">
    <div class="when">Your September letter · Juniper Reformer Studio · delivered October 15</div>
    <h2 style="margin:0;font-size:30px;line-height:1.15;font-weight:800;text-wrap:balance">142 people moved with you this month. 17 regulars could use a hello.</h2>
    <p>Who to reach out to, who to celebrate, and two schedule ideas to test. Everything is as of September 30, so check anything time-sensitive in your own system first.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="big3" aria-label="September at a glance">
    <div class="b"><div class="v num">142</div><div class="l">clients took class</div></div>
    <div class="b"><div class="v num">71%</div><div class="l">average reformer fill, 30 class times</div></div>
    <div class="b"><div class="v num">7 of 24</div><div class="l">intro clients joined by day 42</div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="card" id="s-miss">
    <h2>People we miss</h2>
    <p class="sub">They came weekly or more and hadn't been in for 3 weeks as of Sep 30. By the time this letter arrives, that's two weeks older, so check who's already back or been contacted. You choose who to message.</p>
    <div class="people">
      <div class="person miss"><div class="av">M</div><div><div class="nm">Maya R.</div><div class="why">Twice a week since March · last class Sep 4</div>
        <div class="msg"><small>SUGGESTED TEXT · CHECK BEFORE SENDING</small>Hi Maya! We've missed you on the reformer. If your schedule has changed, let me know what times work and I'll check what's open. No pressure.</div></div></div>
      <div class="person miss"><div class="av">J</div><div><div class="nm">Jenna K.</div><div class="why">Weekly since January · last class Sep 6</div>
        <div class="msg"><small>SUGGESTED TEXT · CHECK BEFORE SENDING</small>Hi Jenna, it's been a few weeks since we saw you. How are things going? Happy to help you find a class that fits this week.</div></div></div>
      <div class="person miss"><div class="av">C</div><div><div class="nm">Carla M.</div><div class="why">Twice a week all summer · last class Sep 8</div>
        <div class="msg"><small>SUGGESTED TEXT · CHECK BEFORE SENDING</small>Hi Carla! Hope your fall is off to a good start. If your schedule changed, tell me what times work better and I'll see what I can hold.</div></div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="note">The other 14 names are on your private working list. A real letter includes up to five personalized messages plus reusable templates.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" id="s-packs">
    <h2>Help them finish their packs</h2>
    <p class="sub">As of Sep 30, 11 clients had packs ending October 20 to 31 with 3 or more classes left: 41 classes already paid for. Those dates fall after this letter arrives, so a reminder can still help. Check the current balance before sending.</p>
    <div class="people">
      <div class="person pack"><div class="av">H</div><div><div class="nm">Hannah B.</div><div class="why">4 classes left · pack ends Oct 20</div></div></div>
      <div class="person pack"><div class="av">R</div><div><div class="nm">Rosa G.</div><div class="why">3 classes left · pack ends Oct 23</div></div></div>
      <div class="person pack"><div class="av">E</div><div><div class="nm">Emily C.</div><div class="why">5 classes left · pack ends Oct 27</div></div></div>
    </div>
    <details><summary>See the other 8</summary><div class="more"><span>Ava S. · 5 left</span><span>Olivia P. · 4</span><span>Zoe K. · 4</span><span>June T. · 4</span><span>Nora J. · 3</span><span>Mia L. · 3</span><span>Ruth M. · 3</span><span>Elle W. · 3</span></div></details>
  </section>

  <section class="card">
    <h2>Worth celebrating</h2>
    <p class="sub">9 clients hit a milestone in September. A shout-out or a handwritten card can be a nice touch, if they're comfortable being recognized.</p>
    <div class="people">
      <div class="person cel"><div class="av">S</div><div><div class="nm">Sofia M. took her 100th class</div><div class="why">Her first class was the grand opening, two years ago.</div></div></div>
      <div class="person cel"><div class="av">K</div><div><div class="nm">Kate R. took her 50th class</div><div class="why">She started with an intro offer in April.</div></div></div>
    </div>
    <details><summary>See the other 7</summary><div class="more"><span>Alma D. · 50th</span><span>Bri S. · 50th</span><span>Cleo T. · 25th</span><span>Dee W. · 25th</span><span>Fay H. · 25th</span><span>Gia N. · 25th</span><span>Ivy O. · 25th</span></div></details>
  </section>

  <section class="card" id="s-class">
    <h2>How full your classes felt</h2>
    <p class="sub">Average share of the 10 reformers booked at each class time in September. W means there was usually a waitlist. Tap a cell for detail.</p>
    <div class="heatwrap"><div class="heat" id="heat" role="img" aria-label="Class fill by day and time. Tuesday and Thursday 5:30pm and Saturday 9:30am were full with waitlists. Weekday noon classes ran 20 to 50 percent full."></div></div>
    <p class="note">The 71% at the top is the simple average of these 30 class times (2,140 ÷ 30). It isn't overall seat use.</p>
    <div class="ins">
      <div><b>Tuesday and Thursday at 5:30pm</b> ran full with about 4 people waiting. <b>Idea:</b> if you have the instructor and room, trial a 6:30pm class those nights, then re-check in 4 weeks.</div>
      <div><b>Weekday noon</b> classes ran 20 to 50% full. <b>Idea:</b> test a lunch-break express class for 4 weeks. Check instructor commitments and costs first.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card" id="s-intro">
    <h2>From first class to regular</h2>
    <p class="sub">Everyone who started the intro offer (3 weeks for $59) between Aug 1 and Aug 19: 24 people, each followed for exactly 42 days, which ends by Sep 30. July comparison: the 23 who started Jul 1 to 19, also at day 42.</p>
    <div class="journey">
      <div class="jrow"><div class="t">Started intro<small>Aug 1 to 19</small></div><div class="jbar"><span style="width:100%"></span></div><div class="n num">24</div></div>
      <div class="jrow"><div class="t">Came 3+ times<small>building the habit</small></div><div class="jbar"><span style="width:67%"></span></div><div class="n num">16</div></div>
      <div class="jrow"><div class="t">Joined by day 42<small>membership or pack</small></div><div class="jbar"><span style="width:29%"></span></div><div class="n num">7</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ins"><div>That's <b>29%</b>, compared with 22% (5 of 23) for July. All 7 who joined came 3+ times. Groups this small swing by chance, so it isn't a trend yet. The <b>9</b> who came 3+ times but hadn't joined are worth a personal invitation. Check first whether any joined since.</div></div>
    <p class="note">Not included: August 20 to 31 starters and the 26 September starters. They'll be measured once they reach day 42.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card" id="s-nums">
    <h2>The money, simply</h2>
    <div class="money num"><span>September <b>$20,396</b></span><span>Up <b>4%</b> from August ($19,612)</span><span>Memberships <b>$10,962</b></span><span>Class packs <b>$7,480</b></span><span>Intro offers <b>$1,534</b> (26 × $59)</span><span>Retail <b>$420</b></span></div>
    <p class="note">$10,962 + $7,480 + $1,534 + $420 = $20,396 gross revenue, before fees and expenses. Not profit.</p>
  </section>

  <p class="foot">Fictional sample by Naté Hailu · made-up studio and example data · drafted with AI assistance · arithmetic checked against the figures shown · a monthly letter, not a live alert list</p>
